  "keyboard": [
    {
      "keys": ["Tab", "Shift+Tab"],
      "effect": "Moves the focus to the trigger and on to the next or the previous control. A disabled select is skipped."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Enter", "Space", "ArrowDown", "ArrowUp"],
      "effect": "Opens the list on the chosen option, or on the first when none is chosen."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["ArrowDown", "ArrowUp"],
      "effect": "In the open list, moves to the next or the previous option, past the disabled ones."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Home", "End"],
      "effect": "In the open list, moves to the first or the last option."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["A letter"],
      "effect": "Moves to the next option that starts with it, open or not."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Enter", "Space"],
      "effect": "In the open list, chooses the option, closes the list and puts the focus back on the trigger."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Escape"],
      "effect": "Closes the list without a change, and puts the focus back on the trigger."
    }
  ],
  "aria": {
    "pattern": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/combobox/examples/combobox-select-only/",
    "rules": [
      "The trigger is a combobox: `aria-expanded` says whether the list is open, and `aria-controls` names the list.",
      "The label is a label element for the trigger: its accessible name. The help and the error are its description, by `aria-describedby`, and a select in error has `aria-invalid` true.",
      "The list is a listbox, its options are options, and the chosen one has `aria-selected` true. A group of options is a group, named by its label.",
      "A disabled option has `aria-disabled` true, and is skipped by the arrow keys.",
      "The chevron, the tick and the loading icon are hidden from assistive technology."
    ]
  },
  "forcedColors": [
    "The edge of the trigger is a real border, which forced colors keep in the system's colors, and in `GrayText` when the select is disabled.",
    "The list's edge is a real border too, so the list stands apart from the page under it, which forced colors paint in the same color as the list.",
    "The option the pointer or the arrow keys are on is outlined in `Highlight`, as its fill is gone.",
    "The line between two groups is a real border, which forced colors keep in the system's color for text, and the group labels keep the groups apart too.",
    "The focus ring is an outline, which forced colors keep. The icons take the system's text color."
  ],
  "motion": [
    "The edge changes color in `motion.duration.fast`, with `motion.easing.standard`. With `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` it changes at once.",
    "The list fades in and grows a little from the trigger in `motion.duration.fast`, with `motion.easing.out`, and goes as it came, with `motion.easing.in`. With less motion it only fades.",
    "The loading icon turns only with `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`."
  ],
  "content": [
    "The label names what is chosen, in sentence case and with no colon: City, Day.",
    "No placeholder. What to choose, or why, goes in the help under the field: Where the conference takes place.",
    "An option is a value, as the reader would say it: Day one, May 10. A group's name says what its options share: Workshops.",
    "An error says how to fix it: Choose the day you are registering for."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The form field around a select, its label, required mark, help and error, is the input spec's, at the same sizes: this spec holds the trigger and its list.",
    "The trigger's chevron is always drawn, so the choice ends past it: the padding at the end is the field's padding, the icon and the control's gap. An icon sits inside the edge, where the choice starts.",
    "An option's leading icon and its description, under its label in the secondary text, are drawn as an implementation draws them and not checked yet. A disabled option is `color.text-faint`, exempt from contrast as WCAG exempts an inactive control.",
    "A gallery draws the open list in place, under its trigger and inside the example, not in a layer at the end of the page, so that a test finds it by the example's id. Its first option is the chosen one, which the list opens on and highlights. The element with the example's id wraps the select itself, its trigger and its list, and never its form field: the form field's label is a slot of its own, which an implementation's list may use for a group's name."
  ],
